WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:07.139
Liar's Dice is a game of bluffing and nerve. Two to six players, and the computer can join in.

2
00:00:07.839 --> 00:00:18.090
Everyone rolls their dice secretly under a cup. Take a peek at your own, and then take turns bidding on how many dice of a certain number are on the entire table.

3
00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:24.409
Like, six fours. That means, I think there are at least six fours across everyone's dice put together.

4
00:00:25.109 --> 00:00:31.848
Every bid has to beat the one before, either with a higher quantity, or the same quantity of a higher number.

5
00:00:31.998 --> 00:00:40.673
Or you can say, liar. Then all the cups are lifted. If the bid was true, the caller loses a die. If it was a bluff, the bidder does.

6
00:00:41.373 --> 00:00:47.916
Ones are wild, and count as any number, unless someone bids on ones. Last player with dice wins.

7
00:00:48.066 --> 00:00:52.365
Know your own dice, guess at everyone else's, and watch who looks nervous.
